CORE gcc-only
main.c
--unwind 4
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assertion sum\(3, 1, 2, 4\) == 7: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ assertion not_a_parameter\(1, 9\) == 9: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
does not handle constant
--
The second argument was taken as the parameter the variadic arguments
follow: `0' aborted symbolic execution ("address_arithmetic does not handle
constant"), and a local variable left the va_list empty.
